--- body ---
## Context

"Easy to try and learn" is a UX quality goal, measured by judgment — but it is
**not** a one-shot audit either: UX drifts as the tool changes, so it needs a
**repeatable, AI-assisted QA process** that re-runs and tracks the product. It
is also the **evidence engine**: how we learn whether speculative feats (e.g.
`erg new --body`) are actually felt, per AGENTS.md "Earning a feature".

## QA process (AI-assisted, repeatable)

AI does the legwork; humans judge.

- **AI persona dry-runs** (per release / per UX-surface change): agents
  role-play the four audiences — beginner, expert trying it out, another
  agent, developer — through the cold-clone *first five minutes* (install,
  create + close a ticket, recover from an induced error) and report friction
  with transcripts. Cheap to re-run, so re-run it.
- **Falsifiable smoke in CI** (every push): the README install steps actually
  execute on a clean image; a "steps/time to first ticket" script stays under
  a budget; help-completeness (every command documented — regression of 0068).
- **Human gate:** judge severity, decide which friction is real and which
  becomes a feat — with the transcript as the attached evidence.

## What to evaluate

- **Time / steps to first ticket** from a cold clone.
- **Orientation:** does `erg` with no args / `erg help` / `erg --help --all`
  orient a beginner? Is the POSIX-first path (just edit a `.erg`) discoverable?
- **Self-describing install:** does `erg init` leave files that explain
  themselves (`AGENTS.md`, spec, `integration.md`)?
- **Error messages:** do they teach (the `filename:line: msg` form from 0124)
  and suggest the fix?

## Output

A findings report per run. Each concrete friction item becomes a **Ready** fix
ticket *with the dry-run transcript attached* — this is how feats earn their
place, pulled by observed friction rather than pushed from the wishlist.

## Relevant files

- `README.md`, `tickets/AGENTS.md`, the `init` assets, help text
  (`helptext.go` / per-command help).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A repeatable AI persona dry-run procedure exists (the four audiences,
      the first-five-minutes script) and has been run once.
- [ ] Falsifiable UX smoke wired into CI (install steps execute, time-to-first
      -ticket budget, help-completeness).
- [ ] The process + cadence are documented so it re-runs — not one-and-done.
- [ ] Friction documented with severity; each actionable item filed as its own
      ticket with the transcript evidence.

## Notes

- **needs-human**, evidence-driven. Prior UX work (closed): 0071–0074
  (UX audit P0–P3), 0124 (error-message format), 0068 (help-completeness
  regression test). Build no feat off this until the friction is observed.
